# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf` decides per developer machine: files committed
# from Windows landed with CRLF in the index while their neighbours were LF
# (several source files and two docs ended up *mixed*), which makes appended
# lines show up as trailing-whitespace errors in `git diff --check` and turns a
# one-line edit into a whole-file diff. LF everywhere also keeps the Linux
# Docker image and shell scripts byte-identical to what CI builds.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only entrypoints keep CRLF; cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only batch files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
